# IFS Cloud / Oracle PL/SQL Developer - Remote Work Type

## About the Project

Directio is a global IT services company. We consult, code, test, deploy, and manage mainly cloud-based and mobile applications, providing around-the-clock support from our offices in Poland, the Philippines, Mexico, and the USA. We prepare our FMCG, retail, automotive, and SaaS clients for the future by accelerating their digital transformation. Operating under the "We Code Success" principle, we prioritize the success of our clients, consultants, and partners.

We are looking for an IFS Cloud / Oracle PL/SQL Developer for our Polish client, a manufacturer of modern acoustic pods and soundproofing solutions for offices. The role involves developing and maintaining IFS Cloud solutions that support the company's key business processes.

This is a direct placement project - not outsourcing!

## Responsibilities

• You will be developing and maintaining solutions within the IFS Cloud system, supporting the organization's business processes and ongoing IT transformation initiatives;
• You will be designing, modifying, and optimizing Oracle PL/SQL queries, procedures, and packages, as well as analyzing and resolving system errors;
• You will be creating and maintaining reports using IFS Report Designer, providing business users with reliable information that supports their day-to-day operations and decision-making;
• You will be developing and maintaining system integrations using REST API, XML, and JSON, while cooperating with the IT team, business users, and process owners;
• You will be supporting business users and participating in the standardization and continuous improvement of IT solutions and development practices.

## Requirements

• Practical experience with IFS Cloud is required; experience limited to IFS Applications 10 will not be sufficient for this position;
• Good knowledge of Oracle PL/SQL and Oracle Database, including the ability to develop and modify queries, procedures, and packages;
• Familiarity with integration technologies and data formats, particularly REST API, JSON, and XML;
• Experience in report development using IFS Report Designer or a similar reporting solution;
• Understanding of business processes in at least one of the following areas: manufacturing, finance, warehousing, logistics, or HR;
• Good command of English, sufficient to work effectively with technical documentation;
• Basic knowledge of Java is considered an advantage;
• Knowledge of Marble or IFS Developer Studio is considered an advantage;
• Experience with Git repositories and an understanding of version control concepts, including branching and pull requests, is considered an advantage;
• Knowledge of clean code principles and basic familiarity with Agile or Scrum methodologies are considered an advantage;
• Awareness of AI tools supporting software development, such as code assistants or code analysis tools, is considered an advantage.

## We Offer

• Salary: 26,000 – 28,000 PLN netto / B2B

## Position Details

**Department:** Database Department  
**Location:** Warsaw  
**Remote Status:** Fully Remote  
**Seniority Level:** Mid-level  
**Jobs - Location:** Poland
