Title: Technology Architecture Intern — Corporate AI Platform (Open)

Location: Remote, hybrid, or in-person at the Rimouski office

Duration: September 8 to December 18, 2026

PG Solutions is laying the groundwork for its corporate future in artificial intelligence, and we want you to be a part of it. Under the supervision of an expert in software development and AI, you’ll have the rare opportunity to participate in a strategic project that will shape how our organization leverages artificial intelligence in its products and services. This internship is not just an observational experience—you’ll make a tangible contribution, leave a lasting impact, and walk away with real-world experience in AI architecture.

Your responsibilities:

- Help define the reference architecture for PG Solutions’ corporate AI foundation;

- Evaluate and compare key technologies (LLM, orchestration, vector storage, APIs, etc.) in line with our AI-first vision;

- Design and build a functional prototype to validate the selected architectural concepts;

- Produce documented, clear, and reusable deliverables for the internal team;

- Propose a technical roadmap to accelerate the deployment of future AI solutions and assistants;

- Actively collaborate with the team in a spirit of openness and knowledge-sharing.

Desired Profile:

Technical Skills:

- Knowledge of the fundamentals of artificial intelligence and machine learning (LLM, RAG, AI agents, etc.);

- Ability to design or analyze software architectures (microservices, REST APIs, cloud);

- Familiarity with Python environments and common AI ecosystems (LangChain, OpenAI, HuggingFace, or equivalents);

- Comfortable with version control tools (Git) and technical documentation.

Analytical Skills:

- Ability to analyze technology options, formulate clear recommendations, and document your conclusions in a structured manner.

Teamwork:

- Comfortable communicating your ideas and receiving feedback;

- Ability to work independently while staying aligned with the team;

- Open-mindedness and a willingness to share what you’ve learned.

Curiosity and Proactivity:

- Strong interest in artificial intelligence and modern architectures;

- Motivation to contribute to something tangible and impactful;

- Resourcefulness, initiative, and a desire to learn by doing.

What We Offer:

- Real impact: You’ll contribute directly to a strategic project—your work will be put to use, not shelved;

- Expert mentorship: An expert will guide you on a daily basis, drawing on their experience in software development and AI;

- Accelerated learning: You’ll be at the heart of the latest AI technologies, applied to a real-world business context;

- Flexibility: Flexible hours and the option to work remotely;

- Collaborative environment: An approachable, transparent, and committed team that values your ideas.

If you’re eager to apply your knowledge of AI and architecture to a project that truly matters, and you’d like to grow in a stimulating environment where your contributions will be recognized and valued, we’d be delighted to welcome you to the team for an internship that will shape your career path.

Harris is committed to an equal employment opportunity program.

Applications from women, people with disabilities, Indigenous people, and visible minorities are encouraged. If you have a disability, you may receive, upon request, assistance with the screening and selection process.

The Harris talent acquisition team never contacts candidates via text message to request confidential information. We encourage all candidates to apply only for posted positions. Selected candidates will be contacted by a Harris manager or a member of the recruitment team to schedule an interview.
